|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||
|
| LAB #7 - Problem 1: Sum of odd and even numbers
| Group 9
| Cabrera, Niles
| Nellas, Aldrin
| Tibayan, Rafael
|
| Reads N and N array values from INPUT, then writes their odd and even sums
| to ODDSUM and EVENSUM.
|
| Registers:
|       R0 = values remaining (starts at N, counts down to 0)
|       R1 = address of the current value (INPUT+4, INPUT+8, ...)
|       R2 = current value
|       R3 = odd sum
|       R4 = even sum
|       R5 = N <= 0 flag at the start, then the current value's parity bit
|
| How odd and even are told apart:
|       ANDC(R2, 1, R5) keeps only bit 0 of the value (1 is ...0001). Bit 0 is
|       1 for odd numbers and 0 for even ones. This also holds for negative
|       numbers in two's complement (-3 = ...11101 is odd, -4 = ...11100 is
|       even), so no division or remainder is needed.
|
| Edge cases:
|       N <= 0 writes 0 to both sums. The loop tests its counter only after
|       the body runs, so without the guard N = 0 would make R0 = -1, and the
|       loop would keep reading past the end of memory until BSim stops with
|       "LD from invalid memory location", never writing the sums. This is
|       the edge case hinted at in the course's sample program.
|       R3 and R4 start at 0, so whatever ODDSUM and EVENSUM held before is
|       overwritten, not added to.
|       Sums that overflow 32 bits wrap around (modulo 2^32).
|       Labels are used as 16-bit signed constants in LD, ST and CMOVE, so
|       the data must stay below address 0x8000.
|
| In BSim (with the data below): the code uses 0x000-0x047, INPUT is at
| 0x19C, ODDSUM at 0x1BC and EVENSUM at 0x1C0.
|
|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||

.include beta.uasm          | include the standard predefined macros

    LD(INPUT, R0)           | R0 = N
    CMOVE(INPUT+4, R1)      | move address of the first array value to R1
    CMOVE(0, R3)            | ensure odd sum is 0
    CMOVE(0, R4)            | ensure even sum is 0
    CMPLEC(R0, 0, R5)       | R5 = 1 if N <= 0, else 0
    BT(R5, DONE)            | if N <= 0, skip to end (both sums stay 0)

LOOP:
    LD(R1, 0, R2)           | load the current value
    ANDC(R2, 1, R5)         | R5 = bit 0 of the value: 1 if odd, 0 if even
    BEQ(R5, EVEN)           | bit 0 is 0 (even): branch to EVEN
    ADD(R3, R2, R3)         | add to running odd sum
    BR(NEXT)                | skip the even addition

EVEN:
    ADD(R4, R2, R4)         | add to the running even sum

NEXT:
    ADDC(R1, 4, R1)         | advance to the next word (each LONG is 4 bytes)
    SUBC(R0, 1, R0)         | subtract from # of values remaining
    BNE(R0, LOOP)           | if # of values remaining > 0, continue loop

DONE:
    ST(R3, ODDSUM)          | store the odd sum (addressed by label only)
    ST(R4, EVENSUM)         | store the even sum (addressed by label only)
    HALT()                  | stop the simulator

|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||

| Data starts at a fixed address so it is easy to find in the BSim window.
. = 0x19C

| INPUT holds N followed by N array values.
INPUT:
    LONG(7)                | array length N; the N values follow
    LONG(5)
    LONG(7)
    LONG(8)
    LONG(6)
    LONG(4)
    LONG(9)
    LONG(3)

| Output sums. Each label reserves one word that the program overwrites.
ODDSUM:
    LONG(0)

EVENSUM:
    LONG(0)
